(3831206, 537584, 50695, '<td valign="top">I very much get the feeling of seeing the back side of something. this easily meets the challenge, regardless of one''s theories of shadow anatomy. :) and not only that, it''s a beautiful, mysterious image. I love it.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-06-25 20:51:21.</i></td>', 'I very much get the feeling of seeing the back side of something. this easily meets the challenge, regardless of one''s theories of shadow anatomy. :) and not only that, it''s a beautiful, mysterious image. I love it.', '2007-06-25 09:56:12.000000', '2007-06-25 21:51:21.000000', 0),
(3831208, 536941, 68256, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone!  Also on a side note no harm was done to the flower or bee :)  This was shot in the garden and yes that 85 1.8 is one awesome lens.  That is God''s backdrop and lighting not mine :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks everyone!  Also on a side note no harm was done to the flower or bee :)  This was shot in the garden and yes that 85 1.8 is one awesome lens.  That is God''s backdrop and lighting not mine :) ', '2007-06-25 09:56:56.000000', NULL, 0),
