(3842559, 536976, 30982, '<td valign="top">I was one of your 8s.  I love the DOF you chose and the tones as well.  The lack of color and the gentleness in this really strike a chord with me.  I think it''s because we associate bees with "busy" yet this seems so peaceful.</td>', 'I was one of your 8s.  I love the DOF you chose and the tones as well.  The lack of color and the gentleness in this really strike a chord with me.  I think it''s because we associate bees with "busy" yet this seems so peaceful.', '2007-06-27 17:04:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842566, 536456, 30982, '<td valign="top">This really is a side we don''t see often - peacocks are so very well known for their plummage, that I find it quite interesting that their backside is also quite showy.  Perfectly titled and very well composed and presented.</td>', 'This really is a side we don''t see often - peacocks are so very well known for their plummage, that I find it quite interesting that their backside is also quite showy.  Perfectly titled and very well composed and presented.', '2007-06-27 17:06:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842573, 537878, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is excellent.  I recall this one clearly from the challenge - I visited with it for awhile.  Sadly, I didn''t have time to comment while voting (took me four days just to vote it all!) but this is one of my top tier pics.</td>', 'This is excellent.  I recall this one clearly from the challenge - I visited with it for awhile.  Sadly, I didn''t have time to comment while voting (took me four days just to vote it all!) but this is one of my top tier pics.', '2007-06-27 17:08:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842576, 536920, 30982, '<td valign="top">Beautiful curves and color and I like the touch of pink from the hanging basket of flowers.</td>', 'Beautiful curves and color and I like the touch of pink from the hanging basket of flowers.', '2007-06-27 17:09:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842580, 536445, 30982, '<td valign="top">I don''t mind the processing - it definitely gives it a different sort of feel which I rather like.</td>', 'I don''t mind the processing - it definitely gives it a different sort of feel which I rather like.', '2007-06-27 17:12:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842592, 537620, 30982, '<td valign="top">Woot!  Congrats on the new personal best!  I like your choice of subject matter here - brings back a lot of good memories of station wagons, pillows, and pajamas in my MUCH younger days.  And I love the dramatic sky.  May be a touch oversharpened/too much contrast - you''ll notice a bit of "halo''ing" on the posts in the back which can be sign of either of the above.  With lines like the posts, you''ll always get a bit of jaggies - very hard to avoid at small sizes like we use here.  A good test is to view it full size, full resolution to see if you''re still getting jaggies - if you are, you know it''s a bit too much sharpening.</td>', 'Woot!  Congrats on the new personal best!  I like your choice of subject matter here - brings back a lot of good memories of station wagons, pillows, and pajamas in my MUCH younger days.  And I love the dramatic sky.  May be a touch oversharpened/too much contrast - you''ll notice a bit of "halo''ing" on the posts in the back which can be sign of either of the above.  With lines like the posts, you''ll always get a bit of jaggies - very hard to avoid at small sizes like we use here.  A good test is to view it full size, full resolution to see if you''re still getting jaggies - if you are, you know it''s a bit too much sharpening.', '2007-06-27 17:15:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842625, 537853, 30982, '<td valign="top">I quite like this - maybe not the "wow" that DPC voters look for but it''s a very good capture that shows the grace and intensity and seriousness with which these young guys take their sport.</td>', 'I quite like this - maybe not the "wow" that DPC voters look for but it''s a very good capture that shows the grace and intensity and seriousness with which these young guys take their sport.', '2007-06-27 17:25:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842670, 536593, 44441, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot, I would have cropped out more of the sky, but that is just my opinion. Overall, very nice photo! Great Job!</td>', 'Very nice shot, I would have cropped out more of the sky, but that is just my opinion. Overall, very nice photo! Great Job!', '2007-06-27 17:42:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842816, 538160, 40718, '<td valign="top">The Technicals: Lighting is good.  It''s even and you controlled the highlight fairly well.  The blacks are black.  That said, the lighting is also not dramatic.  In other words, it merely lights the subject instead of interacting with it.  Focus is an issue.  Your focus plane is on the stem of the plant.  Probably the sharpest focus should be on the petals somewhere.  Using a smaller aperture could have helped (then you would have to use a tripod, but no matter, the flower isn''t moving, you could do a 2 second exposure if you wanted).  Composition is fairly good.  Not centered, but not particularly dynamic.<br/> <br/>The feel: Straightforward.  We see a picture of a flower which has been done fairly well, but it doesn''t provide any "wow".  We take it in quickly, then move on.  There is no reason to linger.<br/> <br/>The game: Flowers have to be done interestingly on DPC to survive.  Look at ursula.  She excels with flowers, so they can be done well, but she also does interesting things with them.  You got a huge number of 5s which means the shot didn''t lack in the technical dept too bad, but didn''t do anything for people either.  Work on some "wow".</td>', 'The Technicals: Lighting is good.  It''s even and you controlled the highlight fairly well.  The blacks are black.  That said, the lighting is also not dramatic.  In other words, it merely lights the subject instead of interacting with it.  Focus is an issue.  Your focus plane is on the stem of the plant.  Probably the sharpest focus should be on the petals somewhere.  Using a smaller aperture could have helped (then you would have to use a tripod, but no matter, the flower isn''t moving, you could do a 2 second exposure if you wanted).  Composition is fairly good.  Not centered, but not particularly dynamic. The feel: Straightforward.  We see a picture of a flower which has been done fairly well, but it doesn''t provide any "wow".  We take it in quickly, then move on.  There is no reason to linger. The game: Flowers have to be done interestingly on DPC to survive.  Look at ursula.  She excels with flowers, so they can be done well, but she also does interesting things with them.  You got a huge number of 5s which means the shot didn''t lack in the technical dept too bad, but didn''t do anything for people either.  Work on some "wow".', '2007-06-27 18:39:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842847, 536976, 40718, '<td valign="top">Technicals: Good.  I don''t see a lot wrong with the technicals.  Nice sharp focus, nice DOF, nice lighting, nice composition.<br/> <br/>The feel: While I get your drift with the B&amp;W application, I may have tried to force attention on the bee through burning/dodging and desaturation of surrounding colors (while keeping them).  It would be another method to give the bee extra attention.  That said, it doesn''t mean this choice was wrong.  It does bring out the texture of the bee nicely.<br/> <br/>The game: I actually like this one and would have expected it to do somewhat better.  It could be that choosing the backside of a bee just wasn''t that great a subject as we like to see their front (or side) in macros.  I almost entered the backside of a dragonfly, but ultimately didn''t because it just didn''t look right to see it from that angle.</td>', 'Technicals: Good.  I don''t see a lot wrong with the technicals.  Nice sharp focus, nice DOF, nice lighting, nice composition. The feel: While I get your drift with the B&W application, I may have tried to force attention on the bee through burning/dodging and desaturation of surrounding colors (while keeping them).  It would be another method to give the bee extra attention.  That said, it doesn''t mean this choice was wrong.  It does bring out the texture of the bee nicely. The game: I actually like this one and would have expected it to do somewhat better.  It could be that choosing the backside of a bee just wasn''t that great a subject as we like to see their front (or side) in macros.  I almost entered the backside of a dragonfly, but ultimately didn''t because it just didn''t look right to see it from that angle.', '2007-06-27 18:48:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842869, 538231, 40718, '<td valign="top">Technicals:  Two things hurt it slightly.  The sharpness is just a bit soft.  That''s from your lens.  Also the brightly lit grass hurts.  Picking another time of day may have been better.  Otherwise I like the composition and the thumb caught my eye in voting.<br/> <br/>The feel:  I like the feel.  A good choice of subject.  The tilted composition also adds to the "broken down" feel.<br/> <br/>The game: I can clearly tell this is at the top of my comment range (4.5-5.5).  The background probably got you in the end along with the softness.</td>', 'Technicals:  Two things hurt it slightly.  The sharpness is just a bit soft.  That''s from your lens.  Also the brightly lit grass hurts.  Picking another time of day may have been better.  Otherwise I like the composition and the thumb caught my eye in voting. The feel:  I like the feel.  A good choice of subject.  The tilted composition also adds to the "broken down" feel. The game: I can clearly tell this is at the top of my comment range (4.5-5.5).  The background probably got you in the end along with the softness.', '2007-06-27 18:53:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3842997, 537712, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals: Lots of 5.5s I''m commenting on.  I can tell the technicals are generally well done for a 5.5 scores.  Not much going against you here.<br/> <br/>The feel: I think I like it.  Composition is nice with the negative space and it''s an interesting idea.<br/> <br/>The game:  One problem for DPC is it''s subtle.  That doesn''t always grab the voter who typically takes 3-5 seconds to vote.  It doesn''t make it a bad pic, but does hurt the pic''s chances for a high vote.</td>', 'The technicals: Lots of 5.5s I''m commenting on.  I can tell the technicals are generally well done for a 5.5 scores.  Not much going against you here. The feel: I think I like it.  Composition is nice with the negative space and it''s an interesting idea. The game:  One problem for DPC is it''s subtle.  That doesn''t always grab the voter who typically takes 3-5 seconds to vote.  It doesn''t make it a bad pic, but does hurt the pic''s chances for a high vote.', '2007-06-27 19:39:14.000000', NULL, 0),
